# Benchmarking & Research Results
# (scripts/results/ is intentionally NOT ignored: README.md, docs/, and
# academic_benchmarks/documentation/ embed images and link data files from it
# as the verified source of truth for SOTA benchmark claims.)

# Eval harness reports -- a number only means something next to the run
# that produced it, so results are never committed.
backend/evals/out/
evals_out/
/evals_out/

# Internal security/engineering audit -- local-only by design. A prior sweep
# committed this once and needed a force-push to undo; ignored here instead
# of relying on every future session remembering not to `git add -A` it.
# Superseded as a work queue by docs/FUTURE_WORK.md (see audit/INDEX.md);
# kept locally as the evidentiary record the findings cite back to.
/AUDIT.md
/audit/

# Local working checklist of open items across the repo, compiled in
# conversation with the user -- a personal work-tracking scratch file, not
# a document meant to ship or be reviewed. Same reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/WHATS_LEFT.md

# Voice-loop root-cause audit and architecture proposal (2026-08-31), written
# against symptoms from a live mic session. A working document whose findings
# belong in .agents/CONTEXT.md once they land, not a deliverable to ship.
# Same reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/VOICE_AUDIT.md

# Execution plan derived from VOICE_AUDIT.md (2026-09-01): 16 buckets across
# 4 phases turning the audit's findings into ordered, verifiable work. A
# personal tracking copy of the approved plan, not a deliverable -- same
# reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/VOICE_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md

# Spec for a richer voice-recording session (2026-09-01), written in response
# to a question about deep-clone quality vs the 64s proof-of-concept corpus.
# Personal working note for planning a future recording session, not a
# deliverable -- same reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/VOICE_RECORDING_SPEC.md

# Survey of brain-inspired / prompt-replacing architectures (2026-09-01),
# written to answer whether prompting can be replaced with something more
# brain-native, and to re-scope vision into Phase 3. A working research note;
# whatever it decides belongs in .agents/CONTEXT.md once it lands, not here.
# Same reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/COGNITIVE_ARCHITECTURE_SURVEY.md

# Partner/investor outreach drafts and pipeline tracker (2026-09-05): named
# real companies and individuals in cold-outreach copy. Internal BD execution
# material, not a project deliverable -- same reasoning as /AUDIT.md above,
# and the same category of content that convention was written to exclude.
/outreach/

# Partnership pitch deck, one-pager, PoC proposals, and due-diligence FAQ
# (2026-09-05), written for specific named target companies. BD/sales
# collateral, not contributor or user documentation. Same reasoning as
# /AUDIT.md above.
/partnership/

# Multi-agent cleanup-orchestration ledger (2026-09-05): phase gates,
# benchmark plans, and cross-agent review transcripts from the internal
# development process, not documentation of the shipped system. Same
# reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/orchestration/

# Patent/IP-candidate analysis (2026-09-05) naming specific mechanisms as
# review candidates with prior-art search vectors -- the document itself
# says this should be reviewed by counsel before open-sourcing. Same
# reasoning as /AUDIT.md above.
/evidence/IP_REVIEW_CANDIDATES.md

# Internal audit reports of the 2026-09-05 cleanup/validation pass itself
# (process telemetry, not reference documentation). Same reasoning as
# /AUDIT.md above.
/REPOSITORY_CLEANUP_REPORT.md
/FINAL_SYSTEM_VALIDATION_REPORT.md

# Live agent identity state (cognitive/identity.py's default when
# IDENTITY_BASE_PATH is unset) -- a SQLite db plus the persona's own working
# copy of personality.json/history.json, written by any local run. Runtime
# output, not source; the seeded defaults it starts from live tracked at
# backend/app/personality.json / history.json.
backend/.identity_state/

# scripts/results/ (root) is the curated benchmark-evidence directory docs
# cite by path -- see the note above. backend/scripts/results/ is not that
# directory; it exists only because a profiling script was once run from
# backend/ instead of the repo root and wrote a stray duplicate there.
backend/scripts/results/
scripts/remote/
.vercel
.env*

